  "description": "How a Webority web head ships its bytes and answers: Brotli-first response compression, static files with the fleet cache policy (versioned assets a year, never immutable), the Cloudflare edge-cache header middleware, the fleet API contract (RFC 9457 problem details for every error including the framework's own, the status and code table, ETag preconditions, retirement headers, idempotent POST and PATCH, the minimum app build announcement), an honest /health endpoint with database and data-protection checks, the paged list contract, and a build-time analyzer that keeps hand-written error bodies out with a shrink-only ceiling.",
